{
  "esm": "1.1.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Relational",
    "description": "Standard-library relational templates (esm-spec §9.7.1 template-library file), the pure-AST definitions of the arg-witness reducers and of value-invention keys and ranks. `argmin(f, n)` / `argmax(f, n)`: the 1-based index in [1, n] of the smallest (largest) candidate value `f`, an expression over the template's loop symbol (`k_argmin_1`, `k_argmax_1`); ties go to the smallest index and a NaN candidate wins at its first occurrence. `argmin_where(f, p, n)` / `argmax_where(f, p, n)`: the same over the candidates passing the predicate `p`, n + 1 when none does. `pair_key(a, b, lo_a, lo_b, n_a, n_b)` and `edge_key(u, v, lo, n)`: scalar integer composite keys (directed, undirected) for a `distinct` key, NaN for an out-of-range component. `rank_of(x, members, n)` / `rank_of_set(x, members, S)`: the 1-based rank of a key among n ascending members, or among the members of the index set S (a derived set's `member_factor`). Core ops only. Import with `expression_template_imports` and invoke with `apply_expression_template`; see docs/content/standard_library.md.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML"
    ],
    "created": "2026-11-07T00:00:00Z",
    "tags": [
      "standard-library",
      "relational",
      "argmin",
      "argmax",
      "arg-witness",
      "value-invention",
      "composite-key",
      "rank",
      "expression-templates"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "esm-spec.md §4.2 (argmin, argmax; NaN in min/max reductions); §9.6 (expression templates); §9.7.1 (template-library files); RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §5.7 rule 6 (smallest-index tie-break). RFC §5.5 and §5.7 rules 1-4 (keys, distinct, rank)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "argmin": {
      "params": [
        "f",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "1-based index k in [1, n] at which the candidate value `f` attains its minimum. `f` is an expression over the loop symbol `k_argmin_1`, which this template binds to each candidate index in turn (write the candidate's value with `k_argmin_1` as its index, e.g. `index(d, i, k_argmin_1)`). Two `faq` reductions: m = min over k_argmin_1 of f, then the smallest k_argmin_1 at which f == m. On a tie the smallest index wins (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §5.7 rule 6). If any candidate is NaN, m is NaN (esm-spec §4.2) and the result is the index of the first NaN candidate. n = 0 gives +Inf (the identity of the `min` reduction). `f` is written twice in the expansion; it must not itself bind `k_argmin_1` for another purpose.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "args": [],
        "output_idx": [],
        "reduce": "min",
        "ranges": {
          "k_argmin_1": [
            1,
            "n"
          ]
        },
        "expr": {
          "op": "ifelse",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "or",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "==",
                  "args": [
                    "f",
                    {
                      "op": "faq",
                      "args": [],
                      "output_idx": [],
                      "reduce": "min",
                      "ranges": {
                        "k_argmin_1": [
                          1,
                          "n"
                        ]
                      },
                      "expr": "f"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "and",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "!=",
                      "args": [
                        "f",
                        "f"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "!=",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "min",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmin_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "expr": "f"
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "min",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmin_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "expr": "f"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "k_argmin_1",
            {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                "n",
                1
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "argmax": {
      "params": [
        "f",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "1-based index k in [1, n] at which the candidate value `f` attains its maximum. `f` is an expression over the loop symbol `k_argmax_1`, which this template binds to each candidate index in turn (write the candidate's value with `k_argmax_1` as its index, e.g. `index(d, i, k_argmax_1)`). Two `faq` reductions: m = max over k_argmax_1 of f, then the smallest k_argmax_1 at which f == m. On a tie the smallest index wins (RFC semiring-faq-unified-ir §5.7 rule 6). If any candidate is NaN, m is NaN (esm-spec §4.2) and the result is the index of the first NaN candidate. n = 0 gives +Inf (the identity of the `min` reduction). `f` is written twice in the expansion; it must not itself bind `k_argmax_1` for another purpose.",
      "body": {
        "op": "faq",
        "args": [],
        "output_idx": [],
        "reduce": "min",
        "ranges": {
          "k_argmax_1": [
            1,
            "n"
          ]
        },
        "expr": {
          "op": "ifelse",
          "args": [
            {
              "op": "or",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "==",
                  "args": [
                    "f",
                    {
                      "op": "faq",
                      "args": [],
                      "output_idx": [],
                      "reduce": "max",
                      "ranges": {
                        "k_argmax_1": [
                          1,
                          "n"
                        ]
                      },
                      "expr": "f"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "and",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "!=",
                      "args": [
                        "f",
                        "f"
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "!=",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "max",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmax_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "expr": "f"
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "max",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmax_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "expr": "f"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "k_argmax_1",
            {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                "n",
                1
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    "pair_key": {
      "params": [
        "a",
        "b",
        "lo_a",
        "lo_b",
        "n_a",
        "n_b"
      ],
      "description": "Directed composite key of the integer pair (a, b) with a in [lo_a, lo_a + n_a) and b in [lo_b, lo_b + n_b): (a − lo_a)·n_b + (b − lo_b), an integer in [0, n_a·n_b). Equal pairs give equal keys and the keys sort in the lexicographic order of the pairs, so a `distinct` over them yields the order and numbering a tuple key would. NaN when a component is out of its range, non-integral or NaN (the value-invention layer refuses a NaN key or join column with `value_invention_key_out_of_range`). Exact while n_a·n_b ≤ 2^53.",
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "and",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "and",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "and",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "and",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "and",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": ">=",
                                "args": [
                                  "a",
                                  "lo_a"
                                ]
                              },
                              {
                                "op": "<",
                                "args": [
                                  "a",
                                  {
                                    "op": "+",
                                    "args": [
                                      "lo_a",
                                      "n_a"
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": ">=",
                            "args": [
                              "b",
                              "lo_b"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "<",
                        "args": [
                          "b",
                          {
                            "op": "+",
                            "args": [
                              "lo_b",
                              "n_b"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "==",
                    "args": [
                      "a",
                      {
                        "op": "floor",
                        "args": [
                          "a"
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "==",
                "args": [
                  "b",
                  {
                    "op": "floor",
                    "args": [
                      "b"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      "a",
                      "lo_a"
                    ]
                  },
                  "n_b"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  "b",
                  "lo_b"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "edge_key": {
      "params": [
        "u",
        "v",
        "lo",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "Undirected composite key of the vertex pair {u, v}, both in [lo, lo + n): `pair_key(min(u, v), max(u, v), lo, lo, n, n)`, so (u, v) and (v, u) give the same key. NaN when an endpoint is out of range, non-integral or NaN.",
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "and",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "and",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "and",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "and",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "and",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": ">=",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "min",
                                    "args": [
                                      "u",
                                      "v"
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  "lo"
                                ]
                              },
                              {
                                "op": "<",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "min",
                                    "args": [
                                      "u",
                                      "v"
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "op": "+",
                                    "args": [
                                      "lo",
                                      "n"
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": ">=",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "max",
                                "args": [
                                  "u",
                                  "v"
                                ]
                              },
                              "lo"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "<",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "max",
                            "args": [
                              "u",
                              "v"
                            ]
                          },
                          {
                            "op": "+",
                            "args": [
                              "lo",
                              "n"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "==",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "min",
                        "args": [
                          "u",
                          "v"
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "floor",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "min",
                            "args": [
                              "u",
                              "v"
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "==",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "max",
                    "args": [
                      "u",
                      "v"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "floor",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "max",
                        "args": [
                          "u",
                          "v"
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "min",
                        "args": [
                          "u",
                          "v"
                        ]
                      },
                      "lo"
                    ]
                  },
                  "n"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "max",
                    "args": [
                      "u",
                      "v"
                    ]
                  },
                  "lo"
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              0,
              0
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "rank_of": {
      "params": [
        "x",
        "members",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "1-based rank of the key x among the n ascending members of a derived index set (its `member_factor` array): 1 plus the number of members below x, the `searchsorted` count of lib/interp.esm. For x a member this is its position; otherwise the position x would be inserted at. The rank of a set's own member is its loop index, which needs no template.",
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          1,
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [
              "members"
            ],
            "output_idx": [],
            "reduce": "+",
            "ranges": {
              "k_rank_of_1": [
                1,
                "n"
              ]
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": ">=",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "members",
                        "k_rank_of_1"
                      ]
                    },
                    "x"
                  ]
                },
                0,
                1
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "rank_of_set": {
      "params": [
        "x",
        "members",
        "S"
      ],
      "description": "1-based rank of the key x among the ascending members of the index set S, read as `members[k]` for k in S (for a derived set, its `member_factor` array): 1 plus the number of members below x, the `rank_of` count with the candidate range `{\"from\": S}` in place of `[1, n]` (esm-spec §9.6.1), so the set's size need not be known when the document is written. S must name a declared index set.",
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          1,
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [
              "members"
            ],
            "output_idx": [],
            "reduce": "+",
            "ranges": {
              "k_rank_of_set_1": {
                "from": "S"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": ">=",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "index",
                      "args": [
                        "members",
                        "k_rank_of_set_1"
                      ]
                    },
                    "x"
                  ]
                },
                0,
                1
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "argmin_where": {
      "params": [
        "f",
        "p",
        "n"
      ],
      "description": "`argmin` over the candidates k in [1, n] for which the predicate `p` holds: the 1-based index of the smallest `f` among them, the smallest such index on a tie, the first NaN index among them when one is NaN, and n + 1 when no candidate passes `p`. `f` and `p` are expressions over the loop symbol `k_argmin_where_1`; `p` is the `filter` of both reductions, so an excluded candidate never competes.",
      "body": {
        "op": "min",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [],
            "reduce": "min",
            "ranges": {
              "k_argmin_where_1": [
                1,
                "n"
              ]
            },
            "filter": "p",
            "expr": {
              "op": "ifelse",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "or",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "==",
                      "args": [
                        "f",
                        {
                          "op": "faq",
                          "args": [],
                          "output_idx": [],
                          "reduce": "min",
                          "ranges": {
                            "k_argmin_where_1": [
                              1,
                              "n"
                            ]
                          },
                          "filter": "p",
                          "expr": "f"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "op": "and",
                      "args": [
                        {
                          "op": "!=",
                          "args": [
                            "f",
                            "f"
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "op": "!=",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "faq",
                              "args": [],
                              "output_idx": [],
                              "reduce": "min",
                              "ranges": {
                                "k_argmin_where_1": [
                                  1,
                                  "n"
                                ]
                              },
                              "filter": "p",
                              "expr": "f"
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "faq",
                              "args": [],
                              "output_idx": [],
                              "reduce": "min",
                              "ranges": {
                                "k_argmin_where_1": [
                                  1,
                                  "n"
                                ]
                              },
                              "filter": "p",
                              "expr": "f"
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                "k_argmin_where_1",
                {
                  "op": "+",
                  "args": [
                    "n",
                    1
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "n",
              1
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
